7] [17592186379260 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379260 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\,$ Read the book, or you won't understand the lecture.\n\nWhich conditional statement is logically equivalent to the disjunctive statement above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379260 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "79056780-76f3-5ac1-9ec9-79ef55cc8595" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379260 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's denote by $A$ and $B$ the following statements:\n\n- $A:$ Read the book.\n\n- $B:$ You won't understand the lecture.\n\nThen, our initial statement can be written as $A∨B,$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬A⇒B.\n$$\n\nThe negation of $A$ can be written as\n\n- $¬A:$ You don't read the book.\n\nTherefore, the given statement is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ If you don't read the book, then you won't understand the lecture." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379265 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379261 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379261 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379261 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186379264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379261 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0274425a-3516-5cf1-ad83-3c6fa0c5f83d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379262 #edb/ref 1080 "If you read the book, then you won't understand the lecture." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379262 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379262 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0d443744-cec7-50fa-b09c-8602760601c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379263 #edb/ref 1080 "If you don't read the book, then you will unders