080 "If you refill the gas, then the car will stop." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379273 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379273 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "655b6822-2da8-54fd-98c3-85d75068c1e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386041 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386041 #edb/ref 1069 "q-102736" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386041 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386041 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the statement $¬P⇒(P∧Q).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386041 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7a2aac01-1463-56cc-bce5-1c99c13e924c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386041 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that\n\n$$\n¬P⇒(P∧Q)≡¬(¬P)∨(P∧Q).\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n¬(¬P)∨(P∧Q)≡P∨(P∧Q).\n$$\n\nFinally, by the absorption law, we have\n\n$$\nP∨(P∧Q)≡P.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $P.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386042 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386042 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386042 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386042 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386042 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386047 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386042 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386042 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386042 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186386044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386042 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7e8c4ca2-b4ee-5544-b0ba-f01f0093c925" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386043 #edb/ref 1080 "Q" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386043 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386043 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "598a18e6-a7e1-5198-85c8-cd85ff5e8356" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386044 #edb/ref 1080 "P" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218638604